# Neo4j Data Modelling Rules

## Node Conventions

- Every node MUST have an `id` property (UUID string).
- Every node MUST have `created_at` (DateTime) and `created_by` (String).
- PascalCase for labels: `ClinicalEpisode`, `Encounter`, `SNOMEDConcept`, `Programme`.
- snake_case for properties: `condition_type`, `confidence_score`, `programme_id`.

## Relationship Conventions

- UPPER_SNAKE_CASE for types: `DOCUMENTS`, `IS_PART_OF`, `HAS_DOMAIN`, `NEXT`.
- Relationships SHOULD have properties when the link carries meaning
  (e.g., `created_at`, `milestone_type`, `confidence`, `condition`).
- Direction matters. Model the natural flow.

## Programme Schema

A Programme is a clinical audit with its own domains, milestones, guidelines, and targets.

```
(:Programme {id, name, description, status})
  -[:HAS_DOMAIN]->(:ValueSet)                 # SNOMED domains to search
  -[:HAS_MILESTONE_DEF]->(:MilestoneDef)      # anchor/milestone definitions
  -[:HAS_EPISODE_TEMPLATE]->(:EpisodeTemplate) # pathway structure
  -[:HAS_GUIDELINE]->(:GuidelineRule)          # compliance checks
  -[:HAS_MEASURE]->(:Measure)                  # quality targets + metrics
  -[:HAS_PIPELINE]->(:PlanDefinition)          # workflow graph definitions
```

## Clinical Graph Schema

Core node types:
- `(:Patient)` -- clinical patient record
- `(:Encounter)` -- GP consultation / clinical event
- `(:SNOMEDConcept)` -- coded concept: `concept_id`, `preferred_term`, `domain`
- `(:ClinicalEpisode)` -- pathway instance: `programme`, `condition_type`, `status`, `confidence`
- `(:GuidelineAlert)` -- guideline compliance alert: `rule_name`, `guideline`, `severity`
- `(:DetectedIssue)` -- quality issue: `issue_type`, `severity`, `suggested_action`
- `(:AbnormalFinding)` -- abnormal test result: `test_type`, `value`, `reference_range`

Core relationships:
- `(Patient)-[:HAS_ENCOUNTER]->(Encounter)`
- `(Encounter)-[:DOCUMENTS {confidence, context}]->(SNOMEDConcept)`
- `(Encounter)-[:IS_PART_OF {milestone_type}]->(ClinicalEpisode)`
- `(Patient)-[:HAS_EPISODE]->(ClinicalEpisode)`
- `(ClinicalEpisode)-[:BELONGS_TO]->(Programme)`
- `(ClinicalEpisode)-[:HAS_ISSUE]->(DetectedIssue)`
- `(Patient)-[:HAS_ALERT]->(GuidelineAlert)`

## Workflow Graph Schema

Pipelines are defined as graph data, not code.

- `(:PlanDefinition)` -- pipeline definition: id, name, version, status, programme.
- `(:WorkflowStep)` -- step config: id, name, capability, timeout_ms, retry_policy,
  input_contract, output_contract.
- `[:HAS_STEP]` -- PlanDefinition owns WorkflowSteps.
- `[:NEXT {condition, priority}]` -- directed edge between steps. `condition` is an
  expression evaluated against the predecessor's output. Null = always fire.

Step capability types reference the Python registry by name:
`shortlist_encounters`, `code_encounters`, `detect_abnormals`, `check_guidelines`,
`detect_anchors`, `build_episodes`, `check_quality`, `calculate_metrics`,
`llm_interpret`, `human_gate`, `trigger_pipeline`.

## Job Execution Schema

- `(:Job)` -- async work unit: id, pipeline_id, programme_id, status, patient_id,
  submitted_at, started_at, completed_at, submitted_by.
- `(:JobStep)` -- per-step execution: id, step_id, capability, status, started_at,
  completed_at, input_hash, output_hash, error.
- `[:HAS_JOB_STEP]` -- Job contains JobSteps.
- `[:USED_PIPELINE]` -- Job links to the PlanDefinition version executed.
- Status lifecycle: `queued` -> `running` -> `completed` | `failed` | `cancelled`.

## AI Model & Invocation Nodes

- `(:AIModel)` -- provider (`spacy_umls`, `openai`, `anthropic`), model_name, status, version.
- `(:AIInvocation)` -- every AI call: model used, input_hash, output_hash, duration_ms, tokens.
- `(:PromptTemplate)` -- versioned prompt templates. `[:SUPERSEDED_BY]` for version chain.

## Immutability

- `(:Approval)`, `(:Change)`, `(:AIInvocation)` nodes are NEVER modified. Append-only.
- `(:Job)` status only moves forward. Never revert a completed/failed job to running.
- `(:PlanDefinition)` with status `active`: immutable. Create a new version to change.
